{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLGlyph"]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlglyph\/equatable-implementations"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Equatable Implementations"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLGlyph\/Equatable-Implementations"},"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Operators","title":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLGlyph\/!=(_:_:)"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLGlyph/!=(_:_:)":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLGlyph\/!=(_:_:)","title":"!=(_:_:)","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlglyph\/!=(_:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"!=","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLGlyph":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The glyph element represents what SMuFL glyph should be used for different variations of symbols that are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"semantically identical. The type attribute specifies what type of glyph is being defined. The element value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies what SMuFL glyph to use, including recommended stylistic alternates. The SMuFL glyph name should"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match the type. For instance, a type of quarter-rest would use values restQuarter, restQuarterOld, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restQuarterZ. A type of g-clef-ottava-bassa would use values gClef8vb, gClef8vbOld, or gClef8vbCClef. A type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of octave-shift-up-8 would use values ottava, ottavaBassa, ottavaBassaBa, ottavaBassaVb, or octaveBassa."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLGlyph","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlglyph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLGlyph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLGlyph","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLGlyph","kind":"identifier"}]}}}